Note the first three principal parts of the following verbs:
αἱρέω, ‘I take, capture, condemn’, and its middle, αἱρέομαι, ‘I take for myself,
choose’;
πάσχω, ‘I suffer, experience, have something happen to me’;
φέρω, ‘I carry, bear, put up with’;
πείθω, ‘I persuade’, and its middle, πείθομαι, ‘I trust, obey’.
